# Allow-list of files vendored from the working tree into this repo.
#
# Format:  <dest path in this repo>   <source path under $TOFU_TREE>
# Blank lines and #-comments ignored. $TOFU_TREE defaults to /home/jack/tofu-unlearning.
#
# WHY AN ALLOW-LIST AND NOT `rsync -a`:
# merge-tables-7b vendored the same tree with a blanket copy and its reproduce/VENDOR_DRIFT.md
# now records "52 files differ, 16 only in the repo, 220 only in home ... the repo copy is not a
# stale snapshot, it is a fork". A blind sync in either direction destroys real work. Only the
# paths below are ever copied, only ever home -> repo, and `sync_from_tree.sh --check` reports
# drift without writing.
#
# Files this repo OWNS (never synced, no source line): the ones marked NEW in PROVENANCE.md —
# submit_expb.sh, collect_expb.py, plot_exp{a,b,c}.py, attribution_stats.py, cluster_env.local.sh,
# stage_hf_cache.sh, the new tests, configs/expb_selectivity_7b.json and the docs.
#
# Files vendored but then EDITED here (self-containment / Exp-B / Exp-C work) carry an
# `edited:` marker. `--check` reports those as EDITED rather than DRIFT, and lists them so a
# future sync is a deliberate merge rather than an overwrite.

